IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc19-s492-21-to-24`

-- ccc19-tests-s492-21-to-24.l4 -- tests for ccc19-s492-21-to-24.l4 (Criminal Code (Canada) ss 492.21 to 492.24).
-- Every expected value is written by hand from the text of the section named beside it, before the run. A failing assertion is a finding.
-- NOTHING is asserted with EQUALS NOTHING (the stable binary has no REFUSE).

§ `s 492.21 -- the definitions apply "in this Part" (sections 492.21 to 492.31)`

-- Inside the Part: the first section, a middle one, 492.3 (which sorts below 492.31) and the last.
#ASSERT `s 492.21 the definitions apply to the provision` (`Provision of the Code` OF 492.21, "") EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 492.21 the definitions apply to the provision` (`Provision of the Code` OF 492.25, "(2)") EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 492.21 the definitions apply to the provision` (`Provision of the Code` OF 492.3, "") EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 492.21 the definitions apply to the provision` (`Provision of the Code` OF 492.31, "(2)") EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Outside the Part: the section before (492.2, Part XV) and the section after (493, Part XVI): not covered.
#ASSERT `s 492.21 the definitions apply to the provision` (`Provision of the Code` OF 492.2, "") EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 492.21 the definitions apply to the provision` (`Provision of the Code` OF 493, "") EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 492.21 the definitions apply to the provision` (`Provision of the Code` OF 515, "(6)") EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 492.21 -- "court" means a court seized of an application for a determination of unreasonable delay`

#ASSERT `s 492.21 court` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a court that is not seized of such an application: "means" closes the definition
#ASSERT `s 492.21 court` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a body that is not a court, though it is seized of an application
#ASSERT `s 492.21 court` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 492.21 court` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 492.21 -- "unreasonable delay" means a delay that exceeds the reasonable time under paragraph 11(b) of the Charter`

#ASSERT `s 492.21 unreasonable delay` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 492.21 unreasonable delay` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the Charter's answer is not known: the definition points outside the text, so it is not covered
#ASSERT `s 492.21 unreasonable delay` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 492.22 -- a finding of unreasonable delay does not deprive the court of jurisdiction`

-- finding made, court seized with those proceedings: the offence, the accused and the offender are each named, and each answer is the text's "does not deprive"
#ASSERT `s 492.22 a finding of unreasonable delay deprives the court of jurisdiction` TRUE TRUE `s 492.22 the offence` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 492.22 a finding of unreasonable delay deprives the court of jurisdiction` TRUE TRUE `s 492.22 the accused` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 492.22 a finding of unreasonable delay deprives the court of jurisdiction` TRUE TRUE `s 492.22 the offender` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- anything else the court has jurisdiction over (a witness, say): not named, so not covered
#ASSERT `s 492.22 a finding of unreasonable delay deprives the court of jurisdiction` TRUE TRUE `s 492.22 anything else` EQUALS NOTHING
-- no finding has been made: the section is not engaged
#ASSERT `s 492.22 a finding of unreasonable delay deprives the court of jurisdiction` FALSE TRUE `s 492.22 the accused` EQUALS NOTHING
-- the court asked about is not seized with those proceedings (the section speaks of "a court seized with those proceedings")
#ASSERT `s 492.22 a finding of unreasonable delay deprives the court of jurisdiction` TRUE FALSE `s 492.22 the accused` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 492.23 -- a court shall not order a stay of proceedings as a result of a finding of unreasonable delay except in accordance with this Part`

-- a stay as a result of the finding, not in accordance with the Part: barred
#ASSERT `s 492.23 the court is barred from ordering a stay of proceedings` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a stay as a result of the finding, in accordance with the Part: the "except" is met, so this section does not bar it
#ASSERT `s 492.23 the court is barred from ordering a stay of proceedings` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a stay that is not as a result of a finding of unreasonable delay (another ground): the section does not speak to it
#ASSERT `s 492.23 the court is barred from ordering a stay of proceedings` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 492.23 the court is barred from ordering a stay of proceedings` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- The regulative rule is exercised with #TRACE (a DEONTIC value cannot be compared in #ASSERT on the stable binary: see NOTES.md, "What the stable binary does not accept").
-- Expected, written before the run: a stay ordered otherwise than in accordance with the Part is a BREACH by the court; a stay in accordance with the Part is not a breach.
#TRACE `s 492.23 the court shall not order a stay of proceedings` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 492.23 order a stay of proceedings as a result of a finding of unreasonable delay` FALSE AT 5

#TRACE `s 492.23 the court shall not order a stay of proceedings` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 492.23 order a stay of proceedings as a result of a finding of unreasonable delay` TRUE AT 5

#TRACE `s 492.23 the court shall not order a stay of proceedings` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 100)

§ `s 492.24 -- rules and principles of the common law continue to apply except insofar as altered by or inconsistent with this Part`

-- a common-law rule, the part in issue neither altered nor inconsistent: continues to apply
#ASSERT `s 492.24 the rule or principle of the common law continues to apply` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- altered by the Part: "except insofar as they are altered"
#ASSERT `s 492.24 the rule or principle of the common law continues to apply` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- inconsistent with the Part: "or are inconsistent with this Part"
#ASSERT `s 492.24 the rule or principle of the common law continues to apply` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 492.24 the rule or principle of the common law continues to apply` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not a common-law rule or principle in respect of a determination of unreasonable delay: the section does not speak to it
#ASSERT `s 492.24 the rule or principle of the common law continues to apply` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 492.24 the rule or principle of the common law continues to apply` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
